2026-10-28T17:30:23.1586862Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgV2p4cf9Y4wS2KtKHTGn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DPZsmvX4rtQ8ST3CGvGAxf","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_read_input_tokens":24853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2814,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ff2900d-a390-479d-912e-23e4afad456a","uuid":"dd6027ca-04af-4e2a-8743-f6e27834e796","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:30:23.156Z","request_id":"req_011CgV2p4J58mp4Z47HTnqrD"}
2026-10-28T17:30:23.1831357Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DPZsmvX4rtQ8ST3CGvGAxf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 16,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/16\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"resource/aws_rolesanywhere_profile: add region argument for enhanced multi-region support\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### Description\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nThe `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` resource does not currently appear to support the enhanced per-resource `region` argument.\\n\\nAWS IAM Roles Anywhere is a regional service with regional endpoints, and profiles may need to be created in more than one AWS Region. Since Terraform AWS Provider v6 added enhanced `region` support to most resources, data sources, and ephemeral resources, it would be useful for `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` to support the same pattern.\\n\\nCurrently, users who want to create Roles Anywhere profiles across multiple Regions still need to use multiple provider aliases. Adding `region` would allow the resource to be managed consistently with other resources that support per-resource Region targeting.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s)\\n\\n- `aws_rolesanywhere_profile`\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n`aws_rolesanywhere_profile` should accept an optional `region` argument.\\n\\nWhen `region` is set, the provider should create, read, update, delete, import, and tag the IAM Roles Anywhere profile in the specified AWS Region.\\n\\nWhen `region` is omitted, the resource should continue to default to the Region configured on the provider.\\n\\nExample:\\n\\n```hcl\\nprovider \\\"aws\\\" {\\n  region = \\\"us-east-1\\\"\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\" \\\"east\\\" {\\n  region = \\\"us-east-1\\\"\\n\\n  name      = \\\"example-east\\\"\\n  role_arns = [aws_iam_role.example.arn]\\n  enabled   = true\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\" \\\"west\\\" {\\n  region = \\\"us-west-2\\\"\\n\\n  name      = \\\"example-west\\\"\\n  role_arns = [aws_iam_role.example.arn]\\n  enabled   = true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n`aws_rolesanywhere_profile` currently rejects `region`:\\n\\n```text\\nError: Unsupported argument\\n\\nAn argument named \\\"region\\\" is not expected here.\\n```\\n\\n### Local Investigation\\n\\nI tested this locally against the provider source.\\n\\n`aws_rolesanywhere_profile` currently has generated service package metadata similar to:\\n\\n```go\\n{\\n    Factory:  resourceProfile,\\n    TypeName: \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\",\\n    Name:     \\\"Profile\\\",\\n    Tags: unique.Make(inttypes.ServicePackageResourceTags{\\n        IdentifierAttribute: names.AttrARN,\\n    }),\\n    Region: inttypes.ResourceRegionDisabled(),\\n}\\n```\\n\\nFor local testing only, I changed that generated metadata to:\\n\\n```go\\nRegion: inttypes.ResourceRegionDefault(),\\n```\\n\\nI also added the v6 SDKv2 fix annotation and excluded `names.AttrRegion` from normal update diff handling:\\n\\n```diff\\n // @SDKResource(\\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\", name=\\\"Profile\\\")\\n+// @V60SDKv2Fix\\n // @Tags(identifierAttribute=\\\"arn\\\")\\n```\\n\\n```diff\\n- if d.HasChangesExcept(names.AttrTags, names.AttrTagsAll) {\\n+ if d.HasChangesExcept(names.AttrRegion, names.AttrTags, names.AttrTagsAll) {\\n```\\n\\nAfter rebuilding the provider locally, Terraform accepted `region` on `aws_rolesanywhere_profile`.\\n\\nThe plan showed two resources using different resource-level Regions:\\n\\n```text\\n# aws_rolesanywhere_profile.east will be created\\n+ resource \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\" \\\"east\\\" {\\n    + name   = \\\"tf-ra-region-test-east\\\"\\n    + region = \\\"us-east-1\\\"\\n  }\\n\\n# aws_rolesanywhere_profile.west will be created\\n+ resource \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\" \\\"west\\\" {\\n    + name   = \\\"tf-ra-region-test-west\\\"\\n    + region = \\\"us-west-2\\\"\\n  }\\n```\\n\\nApply succeeded:\\n\\n```text\\naws_rolesanywhere_profile.east: Creation complete\\naws_rolesanywhere_profile.west: Creation complete\\n\\nApply complete! Resources: 3 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed.\\n```\\n\\nAWS CLI verification showed each profile in the expected Region:\\n\\n```text\\naws rolesanywhere list-profiles --region us-east-1\\n\\ntf-ra-region-test-east\\narn:aws:rolesanywhere:us-east-1:123456789012:profile/...\\n```\\n\\n```text\\naws rolesanywhere list-profiles --region us-west-2\\n\\ntf-ra-region-test-west\\narn:aws:rolesanywhere:us-west-2:123456789012:profile/...\\n```\\n\\nA second Terraform plan was clean:\\n\\n```text\\nNo changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.\\n```\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nThe generated IAM Roles Anywhere service client already appears to support regional targeting through provider/client configuration. The generated `NewClient` code reads `config[names.AttrRegion]` and applies it to `rolesanywhere.Options.Region`.\\n\\nThe blocking issue appears to be that `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` is configured with:\\n\\n```go\\nRegion: inttypes.ResourceRegionDisabled()\\n```\\n\\nrather than:\\n\\n```go\\nRegion: inttypes.ResourceRegionDefault()\\n```\\n\\nBecause `service_package_gen.go` is generated, the final fix likely needs to update the source annotations/generator inputs so that generated service package metadata enables enhanced Region support for `aws_rolesanywhere_profile`.\\n\\n\\n### References\\n\\n- `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` generated service package metadata currently disables enhanced Region support:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rolesanywhere/service_package_gen.go#L37-L45\\n\\n- The generated IAM Roles Anywhere client already reads `config[names.AttrRegion]` and applies it to `rolesanywhere.Options.Region`:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rolesanywhere/service_package_gen.go#L67-L76\\n\\n- Comparable resource `aws_acmpca_certificate_authority` uses `Region: inttypes.ResourceRegionDefault()`:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/acmpca/service_package_gen.go#L67-L78\\n\\n- `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` create logic uses the regional `RolesAnywhereClient(ctx)` and calls `CreateProfile` without a `region` field in the API input:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rolesanywhere/profile.go#L93-L116\\n\\n- `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` update logic currently excludes only tags from `HasChangesExcept`; local testing required also excluding `names.AttrRegion`:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rolesanywhere/profile.go#L170-L188\\n\\n- AWS CLI `rolesanywhere create-profile` supports regional targeting through the standard `--region` global option:\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/rolesanywhere/create-profile.html#global-options\\n\\n- AWS IAM Roles Anywhere API Reference \\u2014 `CreateProfile` request body does not include a `region` field:\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/APIReference/API_CreateProfile.html#API_CreateProfile_RequestBody\\n\\n- AWS IAM Roles Anywhere User Guide \\u2014 IAM Roles Anywhere resources are regional and must be created in the same account and Region to be used together:\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/introduction.html\\n\\n- AWS General Reference \\u2014 IAM Roles Anywhere regional endpoints:\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/rolesanywhere.html\\n\\n- AWS SDK for Go v2 IAM Roles Anywhere package \\u2014 `NewFromConfig` constructs the service client:\\n  https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/service/rolesanywhere#NewFromConfig\\n\\n- AWS SDK for Go v2 IAM Roles Anywhere package \\u2014 `Client.CreateProfile` operation:\\n  https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go-v2/service/rolesanywhere#Client.CreateProfile\\n\\n### Would you like to implement the enhancement?\\n\\nYes\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [\n10\t    \"enhancement\"\n11\t  ],\n12\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:31Z\",\n13\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-06-12T06:34:13Z\"\n14\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ff2900d-a390-479d-912e-23e4afad456a","uuid":"fffa26c9-7819-4a33-a0dc-0b2cd283cec9","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:30:23.172Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 16,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/16\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"resource/aws_rolesanywhere_profile: add region argument for enhanced multi-region support\",\n  \"body\": \"### Description\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nThe `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` resource does not currently appear to support the enhanced per-resource `region` argument.\\n\\nAWS IAM Roles Anywhere is a regional service with regional endpoints, and profiles may need to be created in more than one AWS Region. Since Terraform AWS Provider v6 added enhanced `region` support to most resources, data sources, and ephemeral resources, it would be useful for `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` to support the same pattern.\\n\\nCurrently, users who want to create Roles Anywhere profiles across multiple Regions still need to use multiple provider aliases. Adding `region` would allow the resource to be managed consistently with other resources that support per-resource Region targeting.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s)\\n\\n- `aws_rolesanywhere_profile`\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n`aws_rolesanywhere_profile` should accept an optional `region` argument.\\n\\nWhen `region` is set, the provider should create, read, update, delete, import, and tag the IAM Roles Anywhere profile in the specified AWS Region.\\n\\nWhen `region` is omitted, the resource should continue to default to the Region configured on the provider.\\n\\nExample:\\n\\n```hcl\\nprovider \\\"aws\\\" {\\n  region = \\\"us-east-1\\\"\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\" \\\"east\\\" {\\n  region = \\\"us-east-1\\\"\\n\\n  name      = \\\"example-east\\\"\\n  role_arns = [aws_iam_role.example.arn]\\n  enabled   = true\\n}\\n\\nresource \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\" \\\"west\\\" {\\n  region = \\\"us-west-2\\\"\\n\\n  name      = \\\"example-west\\\"\\n  role_arns = [aws_iam_role.example.arn]\\n  enabled   = true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n`aws_rolesanywhere_profile` currently rejects `region`:\\n\\n```text\\nError: Unsupported argument\\n\\nAn argument named \\\"region\\\" is not expected here.\\n```\\n\\n### Local Investigation\\n\\nI tested this locally against the provider source.\\n\\n`aws_rolesanywhere_profile` currently has generated service package metadata similar to:\\n\\n```go\\n{\\n    Factory:  resourceProfile,\\n    TypeName: \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\",\\n    Name:     \\\"Profile\\\",\\n    Tags: unique.Make(inttypes.ServicePackageResourceTags{\\n        IdentifierAttribute: names.AttrARN,\\n    }),\\n    Region: inttypes.ResourceRegionDisabled(),\\n}\\n```\\n\\nFor local testing only, I changed that generated metadata to:\\n\\n```go\\nRegion: inttypes.ResourceRegionDefault(),\\n```\\n\\nI also added the v6 SDKv2 fix annotation and excluded `names.AttrRegion` from normal update diff handling:\\n\\n```diff\\n // @SDKResource(\\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\", name=\\\"Profile\\\")\\n+// @V60SDKv2Fix\\n // @Tags(identifierAttribute=\\\"arn\\\")\\n```\\n\\n```diff\\n- if d.HasChangesExcept(names.AttrTags, names.AttrTagsAll) {\\n+ if d.HasChangesExcept(names.AttrRegion, names.AttrTags, names.AttrTagsAll) {\\n```\\n\\nAfter rebuilding the provider locally, Terraform accepted `region` on `aws_rolesanywhere_profile`.\\n\\nThe plan showed two resources using different resource-level Regions:\\n\\n```text\\n# aws_rolesanywhere_profile.east will be created\\n+ resource \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\" \\\"east\\\" {\\n    + name   = \\\"tf-ra-region-test-east\\\"\\n    + region = \\\"us-east-1\\\"\\n  }\\n\\n# aws_rolesanywhere_profile.west will be created\\n+ resource \\\"aws_rolesanywhere_profile\\\" \\\"west\\\" {\\n    + name   = \\\"tf-ra-region-test-west\\\"\\n    + region = \\\"us-west-2\\\"\\n  }\\n```\\n\\nApply succeeded:\\n\\n```text\\naws_rolesanywhere_profile.east: Creation complete\\naws_rolesanywhere_profile.west: Creation complete\\n\\nApply complete! Resources: 3 added, 0 changed, 0 destroyed.\\n```\\n\\nAWS CLI verification showed each profile in the expected Region:\\n\\n```text\\naws rolesanywhere list-profiles --region us-east-1\\n\\ntf-ra-region-test-east\\narn:aws:rolesanywhere:us-east-1:123456789012:profile/...\\n```\\n\\n```text\\naws rolesanywhere list-profiles --region us-west-2\\n\\ntf-ra-region-test-west\\narn:aws:rolesanywhere:us-west-2:123456789012:profile/...\\n```\\n\\nA second Terraform plan was clean:\\n\\n```text\\nNo changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.\\n```\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nThe generated IAM Roles Anywhere service client already appears to support regional targeting through provider/client configuration. The generated `NewClient` code reads `config[names.AttrRegion]` and applies it to `rolesanywhere.Options.Region`.\\n\\nThe blocking issue appears to be that `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` is configured with:\\n\\n```go\\nRegion: inttypes.ResourceRegionDisabled()\\n```\\n\\nrather than:\\n\\n```go\\nRegion: inttypes.ResourceRegionDefault()\\n```\\n\\nBecause `service_package_gen.go` is generated, the final fix likely needs to update the source annotations/generator inputs so that generated service package metadata enables enhanced Region support for `aws_rolesanywhere_profile`.\\n\\n\\n### References\\n\\n- `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` generated service package metadata currently disables enhanced Region support:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rolesanywhere/service_package_gen.go#L37-L45\\n\\n- The generated IAM Roles Anywhere client already reads `config[names.AttrRegion]` and applies it to `rolesanywhere.Options.Region`:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rolesanywhere/service_package_gen.go#L67-L76\\n\\n- Comparable resource `aws_acmpca_certificate_authority` uses `Region: inttypes.ResourceRegionDefault()`:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/acmpca/service_package_gen.go#L67-L78\\n\\n- `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` create logic uses the regional `RolesAnywhereClient(ctx)` and calls `CreateProfile` without a `region` field in the API input:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rolesanywhere/profile.go#L93-L116\\n\\n- `aws_rolesanywhere_profile` update logic currently excludes only tags from `HasChangesExcept`; local testing required also excluding `names.AttrRegion`:\\n  https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/main/internal/service/rolesanywhere/profile.go#L170-L188\\n\\n- AWS CLI `rolesanywhere create-profile` supports regional targeting through the standard `--region` global option:\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/rolesanywhere/create-profile.html#global-options\\n\\n- AWS IAM Roles Anywhere API Reference \\u2014 `CreateProfile` request body does not include a `region` field:\\n  https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/APIReference/API_CreateProfile.html#API_CreateProfile_RequestBody\\n\\n- AWS IAM Roles Anywhere User Guide \\u2014 IAM Roles Anywhere resources are regional and must be created in the same account and Region to be used together: